Assertions:
[NAV] URL is {{FRONT_URL}}/company/my-customers/@td(ORG_ACME.id) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] Customer information and Orders sections are both visible on the profile page {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the rendered organization details match @td(ORG_ACME.name) (the clicked row's org) {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the page heading (h1) displays the organization name @td(ORG_ACME.name) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the page heading area shows an organization icon (building placeholder acceptable; a null iconUrl is OK, not a failure) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the Customer information card shows a non-empty account type value (sourced from accountType) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the Customer information card shows a non-empty phone value {OBSERVED}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has a fully seeded address (line1/city/regionName/postalCode/countryCode) — pairs with 050m SR-GQL-036 (backend contract for this exact field set). DOM-VERIFIED (2026-07-17, theme pr-2383): the shipped profile renders a COMPACT ship-to ("<City>, <Region>" only), not the full address block originally assumed. Backend SR-GQL-036 exposes the FULL address (line1/postalCode/countryCode) — the storefront's own salesRepCustomer query deliberately narrows the field selection to city+region for this card. DESIGN-CONFIRM (VCST-5308): is the compact ship-to intended, or should the profile show the full address?

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has an explicit Owner contact resolved as primaryContact (mirrors 050m SR-GQL-019). DOM-VERIFIED (2026-07-17, theme pr-2383): the shipped profile renders the primary contact's NAME ONLY — no email, phone, or photo for the contact. The Customer-information card's "Phone" field is salesRepCustomer.phone (org-level, already covered by SR-CP-005), not primaryContact.phone. DESIGN-CONFIRM (VCST-5308): is name-only primary contact intended, or should email/phone/photo also render?

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has >=2 orders with distinct createdDate (mirrors 050m SR-GQL-022 default sort createdDate:desc).

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has orders in >=2 distinct statuses (mirrors 050m SR-GQL-033 salesRepOrderStatuses). Feature absent on shipped pr-2383 — DESIGN-CONFIRM (VCST-5308): is order-status filtering in scope or deferred? Currently display-only badges (click expands a tooltip; no list filtering). Left Draft pending the design decision — assertions NOT rewritten to match the current absence.

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has at least one order with status Cancelled and a non-zero total. Storefront culture switched to a non-English locale. Pairs with 050m SR-GQL-031 (statusDisplayValue) and SR-GQL-037 (total.formattedAmount, nested MoneyType — CONFIRMED via Phase-5 live introspection 2026-07-17) — this case only bridges the rendered UI to those already-verified API contracts. Fails on pr-2383: profile Orders query selects raw `status`, not `statusDisplayValue` — status badge stays English under /de. Product bug, not a test defect; assertion intentionally left as-is (correctly grounds the desired behavior and catches the real bug).

[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has >=1 order with a known number, createdDate, and itemsCount > 0 (mirrors 050m SR-GQL-022). DOM-VERIFIED (2026-07-17, theme pr-2383): the profile Orders table renders the order number WITHOUT a "#" prefix — omitted here vs the list-page (089 SR-FE-004) and order-details conventions; logged as a cosmetic inconsistency, not a functional defect.

Assertions:
[DOM] each order row shows a non-empty order number (no "#" prefix in this table, unlike 089's list-page convention — see note) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] each order row has a formatted date visible, e.g. "Jul 17, 2026" (no raw ISO timestamp) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] each order row has a non-zero item count visible {OBSERVED}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
[PRE:SIGNIN_AS:SR_REP_PRIMARY]
@td(ORG_ACME.id) has >=1 order. Carries over the ordering-asymmetry/403 concern documented at the list-page layer in 089 SR-FE-006 — unresolved there, so unresolved here.

Steps:
